workedExamples.question_text:
A stormwater network has the pipe capacities shown, in kL/h. Each arrow shows the permitted flow direction.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (3,3);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\coordinate (T) at (6,1.5);
\draw[->] (S)--(A) node[midway,above left] {$60$};
\draw[->] (S)--(B) node[midway,below left] {$40$};
\draw[->] (A)--(T) node[midway,above right] {$50$};
\draw[->] (B)--(T) node[midway,below right] {$70$};
\draw[->] (A)--(B) node[midway,right] {$20$};
\fill (S) circle (2pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill (A) circle (2pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill (T) circle (2pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Determine whether the network meets demand of $115\text{ kL/h}$. Which single pipe could be enlarged, and by how much, to meet this demand?

development.question_text:
A network with source $S$ and sink $T$ has edge capacities: $SA = 40, SB = 30, AT = 35, BT = 45, AB = 10$ ($A\to B$).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.5);
\coordinate (A) at (2.5,2.7);
\coordinate (B) at (2.5,0.3);
\coordinate (T) at (5.0,1.5);
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$40$};
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (B) node[midway, below left] {$30$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$10$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (T) node[midway, above right] {$35$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (T) node[midway, below right] {$45$};
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill (T) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The council upgrades pipe $SA$ from $40$ to $55$.
Find the new maximum flow through the network.
